---
description: Bump versions and CHANGELOG together — never one without the other. Ship tags must be SSH-signed.
globs: CHANGELOG.md,project.yml,README.md
alwaysApply: true
---

# Versioning

Follow SemVer (`MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`). One version per app.

| Change | SemVer bump |
|--------|-------------|
| User-facing feature (compatible) | MINOR |
| Bug / fix | PATCH |
| Breaking | MAJOR |
| Docs / chore / internal-only | none |

## Version bump = CHANGELOG entry (same commit)

**Never bump `MARKETING_VERSION` without updating root `CHANGELOG.md` in the same commit.**

1. Add a `## X.Y.Z — YYYY-MM-DD` section at the top (below the title).
2. Group bullets under `### Added`, `### Fixed`, `### Changed`, or `### Breaking`.
3. One section per release; do not edit past sections except typos.

## Files to keep in sync

| File | Field |
|------|-------|
| `project.yml` | `MARKETING_VERSION`, `CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION` |
| `QuotAI.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj` | regenerate via `xcodegen generate` after `project.yml` |
| `README.md` | download link / version callouts that name the shipped build |
| Git tag | `vX.Y.Z` (signed — see below) |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | new top section for the bump |

Increment `CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION` on every release build.

After bumping version, run `python3 ~/dev/scripts/update-dev-index.py` to refresh `~/dev/INDEX.md`.

## Git

- Do not land versioned work on `main` — branch `feat/…`, `fix/…`, or `hotfix/…` first.
- Tag the release commit with a **signed** annotated tag `vX.Y.Z` when shipping (see below).
- Docs/chore/internal-only: no version bump, no CHANGELOG entry.
- Do **not** retag old releases unless the user explicitly asks. From the next release onward, signed tags only (e.g. leave unsigned `v0.9.4` as-is).

## Signed release tags (required)

GitHub **Verified** on the Tags page requires a cryptographically signed tag. Unsigned annotated tags and lightweight tags do **not** count (lightweight may look Verified only because the pointed-to merge commit is GitHub-signed — do not rely on that).

**Always** create release tags as:

```bash
git tag -s "vX.Y.Z" -m "X.Y.Z"
git verify-tag "vX.Y.Z"   # must succeed before push
git push origin "vX.Y.Z"
```

**Never** for a ship tag:

- `git tag vX.Y.Z` (lightweight)
- `git tag -a` without signing
- Pushing a tag when `git verify-tag` fails
- Falling back to unsigned if signing is misconfigured — **stop** and fix signing first

### One-shot signing (prefer when global git config is unset)

Do **not** change global git config unless the user asks. Prefer per-invocation flags:

```bash
ssh-add --apple-use-keychain ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_github
git -c gpg.format=ssh -c user.signingkey="$HOME/.ssh/id_ed25519_github" tag -s "vX.Y.Z" -m "X.Y.Z"
```

Local verify needs an allowedSigners file:

```bash
ALLOWED=$(mktemp)
echo "marotron@gmail.com $(cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_github.pub)" > "$ALLOWED"
git -c gpg.format=ssh -c gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile="$ALLOWED" verify-tag "vX.Y.Z"
rm -f "$ALLOWED"
```

### Optional permanent setup (only if the user wants git config written)

```bash
git config --global gpg.format ssh
git config --global user.signingkey ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_github
git config --global tag.gpgsign true
```

GitHub → Settings → SSH and GPG keys → **New SSH key** → Key type **Signing Key** (same pubkey can already exist as Authentication). Account-wide; one signing key covers QuotAI and MailGent.

Closeout must propose the signed form, e.g. `Proposed tag: git tag -s vX.Y.Z -m "X.Y.Z"`.

## Closeout (after a bump)

**Do not** stage/commit/tag until the user confirms.

```
Version closeout — vX.Y.Z
Branch: feat/… or fix/…
Proposed tag: git tag -s vX.Y.Z -m "X.Y.Z"

Proposed commit message:
<subject>

<body>

If you are happy with these changes, say so and I will stage and commit.
I will not commit until you confirm.
```
